class.description:
[CgamePlatformServices] is everything the game needs from the host platform that is not rendering or input mapping: integrity-checked saves with backup recovery, achievements, presence, entitlements, parental restrictions, text input, and the session rules that console certification asks for (pause on controller loss, pause on suspend, end the session on sign-out).
The singleton talks to a [CgamePlatformBackend]. If none was set, a [CgameDesktopPlatformBackend] is created on first use. The singleton attaches a small helper node to the scene tree so that [constant MainLoop.NOTIFICATION_APPLICATION_PAUSED] suspends and [constant MainLoop.NOTIFICATION_APPLICATION_RESUMED] resumes the backend. Instances created with [code]CgamePlatformServices.new()[/code] do not attach themselves; forward notifications with [method handle_notification].
Saves are stored as [code]CGS1:<hash>:<json>[/code]. [method load_game] verifies the hash, falls back to the backup copy when the main file is missing or damaged, and reports which source was used.
[codeblock]
var services = Engine.get_singleton("CgamePlatformServices")
services.start_session()
if services.save_game("slot1", {"level": 3}) == CgamePlatformServices.SAVE_OK:
	print("saved")
var result = services.load_game("slot1")
if result["result"] == CgamePlatformServices.SAVE_OK:
	print(result["data"])
[/codeblock]
